{"ts": 0.333627, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mStage 4 cleared\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nYou can now\r\n\r\n  ask if a program is there    \u001b[92mcommand -v\u001b[0m\r\n  count, order, filter         \u001b[92mwc       \u001b[0m \u001b[92msort     \u001b[0m \u001b[92mgrep\u001b[0m\r\n  take the first lines, count out \u001b[92mhead     \u001b[0m \u001b[92mseq\u001b[0m\r\n  chain commands               \u001b[92m|\u001b[0m\r\n  send output to a file        \u001b[92m>        \u001b[0m \u001b[92m>>\u001b[0m\r\n  read input, match many names \u001b[92m<        \u001b[0m \u001b[92m*\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nNext: Stage 5 · Ready for vimtutor\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m to go on, or \u001b[92mquit\u001b[93m to stop here. Your place is saved.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 554}
{"ts": 0.333748, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.336558, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(Stage 5)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(stop here, place saved)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 135}
